<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christoph, Duke of Württemberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1515–1568</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Christopher, Duke of Württemberg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Christoph was Duke of Württemberg from 1550 to 1568, succeeding his father Ulrich. With the reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-brenz">Johannes Brenz</a> he organised a Lutheran territorial church, set out in the Great Church Order of 1559, and created a system of schools and monastic seminaries to train clergy. He worked with the estates and was one of the most respected Protestant princes of his time.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christoph-duke-of-wurttemberg.jpg" alt="Christoph, Duke of Württemberg" width="320" height="624" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abraham del Hele · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abraham_Hel_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
